            <div xml:id="d605">

                <pb facs="0786" n="692" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg692"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.75/9: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Moore</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-08-26T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 26,
                                1924—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>39. Exclusive telephone rights in Spain have been given to American telephone
                    interests who were assisted by Embassy in winning concession which involves
                    about $8,000,000. Announcement must not be made in United States but will soon
                    be made from Madrid.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
